task(EXP-LL-01-P1):
  title    = "EXP-LL-01 P1 — Ω Doughnut (Raworth social floor / ecological ceiling)"
  status   = done
    // DESIGN PIVOT (honest geometry): per-sector floor/ceiling box is CONVEX (Q1
    // passes trivially — no drama); the radial annulus is an aggregation artifact.
    // GENUINE non-convexity = wealth-channel coupling: Ω_econ = Ω_A(extractivist)
    // ∪ Ω_B(diversified), possibly disjoint (transition valley violates the floor)
    // → b0=2 measurable via VR/ripser. H_LL2 reformulated with 4 predictions incl.
    // constructive convexity counterexample + first real use of Betti machinery.
    // DS impl: P1a-P1d in design §5 (omega_econ.py + calibration + counterexample + topology).
  priority = alta
  date     = "2026-06-28"
  context:
    "Define the 'just ring' around market-clearing p* using Raworth's Doughnut:
     social floor (minimum viable sectors) + ecological ceiling (resource limit).
     Test H_LL2: does the tâtonnement equilibrium land inside the ring?
     Spoiler: probably not (copper dominates; agriculture/manufacturing depressed).
     Q1 Fierro for economic domain: Ω is an annulus → non-convex → Q1 fails.
     This is the first domain where Q1 deliberately fails by design."
  model    = "Opus (geometric design of Ω + H_LL2 formulation)"
  audit_2026_08_02: "CONFIRMED genuinely still open (2026-08-02 debt audit): grep found NO
      omega_econ.py anywhere in the repo, only the design doc. Over a month with a written
      design (P1a-P1d in design §5) and zero implementation, despite sibling tasks from the
      SAME batch (EXP-LL-01-COPPER, EXP-LL-01-COUPLE) both landing within days. Dispatch-ready:
      implement P1a-P1d exactly as designed in omega_doughnut_design.vsm §5 — omega_econ.py +
      calibration + counterexample construction + VR/ripser topology (b0=2 test). done_when:
      H_LL2 predictions in the design doc get real measured values, not just the design."
  depends_on = []
  unblocks = [ITEM_22_close, EXP-S2-01]

